<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a telescopic conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A belt or roller conveyor that extends and retracts to reach into truck trailers, containers, and railcars from the dock. Nested sections slide inside one another to reach deep into the trailer. Caljan states its Classic can cut loading and unloading times in half compared with manual handling.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How far can a telescopic conveyor extend?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Reach depends on the number of nested sections. Caljan offers its Classic telescopic conveyor in multiple section configurations reaching up to 16 meters (about 52 feet), and markets a 5-section Performer model for longer reach. More sections add reach, weight, and cost. Size the extension to the deepest trailer or container the dock serves.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Belt vs. roller telescopic conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Belt: handles all product shapes (bags, polybags, irregular items), costs more. Roller: handles flat-bottom cases and totes, costs less. Belt versions dominate because dock operations handle mixed product streams. Roller versions suit facilities shipping only uniform cases.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How much time does a telescopic conveyor save?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The main gain is removing the walk between the trailer and the dock. Caljan states its Classic telescopic conveyor can cut truck loading and unloading times in half compared with manual handling. The belt also takes over carrying, which reduces fatigue and the handling that leads to dropped or thrown cartons. Results depend on product weight, trailer length, staffing, and whether the conveyor is used for loading, unloading, or both. Run a time study on your own docks before and after to measure the change.</p>

</div>
</div>
